<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Little Aden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Little <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> is a rocky peninsula on the western side of the bay of Aden in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> bought it from the Aqrabi sheikh in the 1860s and attached it to the Aden Settlement. In 1954 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bp">Anglo-Iranian Oil Company</a> opened a large refinery there, which later passed to the Yemeni state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/little-aden.jpg" alt="Little Aden" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahmedxalkatheri · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MallaDistrict.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
